  ],
  "equipment_type": "Cooling tower and condenser pump plant controller",
  "applies_to": "Armstrong Design Envelope Integrated Tower Controller for the condenser water side: up to 5 cooling towers (fans, inlet/outlet isolation valves) and 5 condenser water pumps.",
  "summary": "The ITC 9521 sequences cooling towers and condenser water pumps. Its BACnet object list covers start/stop, alarm reset, tower water temperatures, condenser flow, outdoor temperature and humidity, bypass valve positions, pump and fan drive data, run hours, duty/standby and running status, valve states, alarms and Hand/Auto overrides.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": "BACnet communication interface Rev 17.111",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The data-points sheet titles the table BACnet but does not say whether it is BACnet IP or MS/TP.",
    "Mode/Selector AVs: 0 = Not Used, 1 = Hand, 2 = Off, 3 = Auto (writes limited to 1-3). Duty/standby, running status and valve position status AIs are coded; the codes are in each point's states.",
    "Units for temperatures, pressures and flows follow the controller's unit setting (the PDF lists the options).",
    "Some Speed Reference/Speed Feedback pairs share one range cell in the PDF; both are given 0-100 %.",
    "The PDF table is on pages 10-15."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "The ITC 9521 runs the condenser water side: cooling towers, condenser pumps, tower isolation valves and bypass valves. Start and stop it with BO 1 Remote Start, read BI 1 Plant Status, tower water temperatures, condenser flow and outdoor conditions, and reset alarms with BO 2. Per-pump and per-fan modes, hand speeds and valve overrides are available.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 1",
        "name": "Remote Start",
        "why": "Start/stop from the BMS (1 = start)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 2",
        "name": "Alarm Reset",
        "why": "Reset alarms (positive edge)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1",
        "name": "Plant Status",
        "why": "Controller on/off status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Leaving Tower Water Temp",
        "why": "Condenser water leaving the towers"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "Entering Tower Water Temp",
        "why": "Condenser water entering the towers"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "Condenser Flow",
        "why": "Condenser water flow"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "Outside Air Temp (Dry Bulb)",
        "why": "Outdoor dry-bulb temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 128",
        "name": "Cooling Tower Water Low Level Alarm",
        "why": "Tower basin low water level"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BO 1 Remote Start (0 = Stop, 1 = Start) starts and stops the controller from the BMS. The data-points sheet says nothing more about local/remote selection.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The data-points sheet does not give the device instance, MAC address, baud rate or IP settings; get them from the controller setup."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "BO 2 Alarm Reset acts on a positive edge (0 to 1).",
      "Mode/Selector AVs accept only 1-3 when written (1 = Hand, 2 = Off, 3 = Auto); Hand runs the pump or fan at its Hand Speed AO.",
      "Hand/Auto switch BVs and Hand Command BVs override the valve sequence; leave them in Auto for normal operation.",
      "The Sensorless Head points are printed with kW as the unit; treat that unit with care."
    ]
  },
  "source": {
